Below is a **complete, self‑contained C# solution** that shows how you can build an **autonomous traffic‑light control system** that is split into three **isolated, testable modules**:

| # | Module | Responsibility |
|---|--------|-----------------|
| 1 | **IntersectionVehicleSensorIngester** | Receives raw sensor events, maintains per‑lane vehicle queues, and publishes the current queue snapshot. |
| 2 | **AdaptiveTimingOptimizationEngine** | Consumes the queue snapshot and, using a simple heuristic, produces a **green‑time plan** for each traffic movement. |
| 3 | **HardwareSignalController** | Takes the timing plan and drives the physical (or simulated) traffic‑light hardware – turning lights red, yellow and green at the right moments. |

The three modules communicate only through **plain‑old‑C# interfaces**, so you can swap any implementation (e.g., replace the simulated hardware with a real PLC driver) without touching the other parts.

---

## 1. Project Layout

```
/TrafficControlSystem
│   Program.cs                <-- entry point / orchestrator
│
├─/Core
│   IQueueSnapshot.cs
│   ITimingPlan.cs
│   IHardwareSignal.cs
│
├─/Modules
│   /SensorIngester
│        IIntersectionVehicleSensorIngester.cs
│        IntersectionVehicleSensorIngester.cs
│
│   /TimingEngine
│        IAdaptiveTimingOptimizationEngine.cs
│        AdaptiveTimingOptimizationEngine.cs
│
│   /SignalController
│        IHardwareSignalController.cs
│        HardwareSignalController.cs
│
└─/Models
        LaneId.cs
        Direction.cs
        LightState.cs
        SensorEvent.cs
        TimingPlan.cs
```

> **Tip:** All files can be placed in a single `.cs` file for a quick demo – the namespaces below already reflect the folder structure.

---

## 2. Shared Types (`Models`)

```csharp
using System;

namespace TrafficControlSystem.Models
{
    /// <summary>Unique identifier for a lane (e.g., N‑North, S‑South, …)</summary>
    public readonly record struct LaneId(string Id);

    /// <summary>Two‑way movement – used to group opposite lanes that share a signal.</summary>
    public enum Direction { NorthSouth, EastWest }

    /// <summary>Traffic‑light colour per lane.</summary>
    public enum LightState { Red, Yellow, Green }

    /// <summary>Raw event coming from a loop detector, camera, radar, …</summary>
    public sealed record SensorEvent(LaneId Lane, DateTime Timestamp);

    /// <summary>Snapshot of all lane queues at a point in time.</summary>
    public sealed record QueueSnapshot(
        DateTime CapturedAt,
        IReadOnlyDictionary<LaneId, int> LaneQueueLengths);

    /// <summary>Green‑time allocation for a movement direction.</summary>
    public sealed record TimingPlan(
        DateTime GeneratedAt,
        IReadOnlyDictionary<Direction, TimeSpan> GreenDurations);
}
```

